    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is anchored by **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 85.94 against Randy V\u00e1squez. With a projected leadoff spot and a favorable SP xERA of 4.92, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary target for stolen base production, aided by a significant platoon advantage. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** offers high upside at 75.98; he benefits from the most favorable park factor (+14%) and platoon matchup (+14%) of the day, making him a critical start against Freddy Peralta. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Tyler Soderstrom** round out our top-tier plays, both exploiting the porous nature of their respective matchups to push into the 69\u201371 range.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the middle-infield/bench pivot, where **Zach McKinstry** narrowly missed the cut with a 38.04 score. While his potential for stolen bases against a slower-to-the-plate pitcher offered a minor boost, he fell just short of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor,\" ultimately benched in favor of the higher-upside profiles of **Travis Bazzana** and **Cole Young**. We are keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley**, whose 57.44 projection is tempered by a concerning 44% rain risk at the stadium. While his matchup against Gusto is theoretically strong, any weather delay could force a late-game rotation pivot to our deeper reserves like **Dalton Rushing** or **Edwin Arroyo** should conditions deteriorate. \n\nFinally, note that **Seiya Suzuki** faces the toughest task today, drawing the elite arm of Tarik Skubal (2.67 xERA). Despite the difficult matchup, his secure spot in the order and park factors keep him just above the marginal threshold at 51.26. With **Trevor Story** remaining on the IL and both **Jose Caballero** and **James Wood** unavailable for today's slate, we are relying on our core depth\u2014including the bats of **Isaac Paredes** and **Josh Naylor**\u2014to maintain our pace in the 5x5 race. We continue to monitor the status of **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot starts later this week as we manage our game caps.",
